rh264 source licensing and table provenance
==========================================

Original implementation
-----------------------
The original decoder code, public interface, bit-depth kernels and table
generator are licensed under MIT (COPYING.MIT). The original-code license
was explicitly authorized by the maintainer on 2026-10-13.

OpenH264 data
------------
The CAVLC tables in rh264.c and the generated CABAC initialization data in
rh264_cabac_tables.h contain data adapted from Cisco OpenH264. These portions
remain BSD-2-Clause, with the Cisco copyright, conditions and disclaimer
retained in the source and COPYING.OpenH264. The MIT permission applies to
the original code, not as a replacement for Cisco's notice. Include both
COPYING files with binary distributions that include this decoder.

Pinned OpenH264 revision: 1bca62311e447fd9c39fc93de2c4b96cd5ce971c
Repository: https://github.com/cisco/openh264

CAVLC source: codec/encoder/core/src/encoder_data_tables.cpp
  rh264_ct_{len,code} and rh264_ctc_{len,code}: g_kuiVlcCoeffToken
  rh264_tz_{len,code}: g_kuiVlcTotalZeros
  rh264_rb_{len,code}: g_kuiVlcRunBefore
  rh264_cdctz_{len,code}: g_kuiVlcTotalZerosChromaDc
These values were compared exhaustively with the pinned source. The separate
4:2:2 chroma-DC tables implement H.264 Tables 9-5 and 9-9; they are not present
in the pinned OpenH264 source and are not described as OpenH264 extractions.

CABAC source: codec/common/src/common_tables.cpp
  Base contexts 0..459: g_kiCabacGlobalContextIdx, all four variants.
  Unused I-slice CTX_NA entries are represented as zero pairs.
  Extended contexts 460..1023 are generated by reusing base-context ranges.
  The 25 ranges in generate_cabac_tables.py correspond to H.264 (08/2024),
  Tables 9-25..9-33. All 564 extended contexts, in all four variants, were
  compared with those normative tables; the printed 641 next to context 497
  in Table 9-26 is interpreted as 541, following that column's 528..571 range.

Earlier revisions copied the extended CABAC data from FFmpeg's
libavcodec/h264_cabac.c. That embedded block has been replaced by the output
of the pinned BSD-source generator. No FFmpeg file is an input to generation.
All 4096 output pairs remain numerically identical, so this replacement does
not change decoding behavior. This describes the current source; it does not
relicense or remove the provenance of earlier revisions or distributions.

Reproduction
------------
Download the pinned common_tables.cpp identified by SOURCE_URL in the
generator. Then, from this directory:

  python3 generate_cabac_tables.py /path/to/common_tables.cpp --check

Omit --check to regenerate rh264_cabac_tables.h. The script checks the complete
input SHA256 before parsing, verifies table dimensions and range coverage,
and needs only the Python standard library. Generation does not access the
network. The generated header carries the full BSD notice so that it can be
vendored with the decoder.

Normative reference:
https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-H.264-202408-S/en

This source/license audit does not grant patent rights or constitute a legal
clearance of an upstream project's complete distribution.
